{"id": "NYSEDREGENTS_2015_4_29", "question": "What is the main source of energy for all of the organisms in most food chains?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): sunlight", "B): water", "C): green plants", "D): decomposers"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. Most food chains start with green plants, which are producers.\n2. Producers use sunlight to create energy through photosynthesis.\n3. This energy is then passed on to consumers (herbivores, carnivores, and omnivores) when they eat the plants.\n4. Decomposers break down dead organisms and return nutrients to the soil, but they do not provide energy for the food chain.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.8690776414587162e-05, 2.1884650536208028e-08, 1.427058435865547e-07, 9.615443996580098e-10], "initial_probs": [0.0006194123416207731, 5.358966518542729e-06, 5.0844460929511115e-05, 5.648309411299124e-07], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "NYSEDREGENTS_2015_4_29_step_1", "global_job_index": 922, "cot_step": "Most food chains start with green plants, which are producers.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Most food chains start with green plants, which are producers.", "2.", "Producers use sunlight to create energy through photosynthesis.", "3.", "This energy is then passed on to consumers (herbivores, carnivores, and omnivores) when they eat the plants.", "4.", "Decomposers break down dead organisms and return nutrients to the soil, but they do not provide energy for the food chain."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}, "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "NYSEDREGENTS_2015_4_29_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0005_rs=1001_pos=True_ff2=False_critical_lora_causal_cot_i09_unfiltered_pos_s0/NYSEDREGENTS_2015_4_29_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"b