{"id": "Mercury_SC_416529", "question": "Why do most of the leaves of forest trees grow at the top of the tree?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): to scatter seeds", "B): to capture sunlight", "C): to shade the trunk", "D): to collect water"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The main function of leaves is to perform photosynthesis, which is the process of converting light energy into chemical energy (sugar) for the plant.\n2. Sunlight is essential for photosynthesis, as it provides the energy needed to drive the chemical reactions.\n3. Trees grow taller to reach higher levels of sunlight, especially in dense forests where sunlight is limited.\n4. By growing leaves at the top of the tree, the leaves can capture more sunlight and maximize the plant's ability to perform photosynthesis.", "initial_cot_probs": [8.590412825526528e-10, 1.3004641914449167e-05, 6.69022004462505e-10, 7.990328537710312e-11], "initial_probs": [8.747330326741576e-08, 0.0005520167178474367, 4.4422606038097e-07, 7.71949189015686e-08], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_416529_step_1", "global_job_index": 542, "cot_step": "The main function of leaves is to perform photosynthesis, which is the process of converting light energy into chemical energy (sugar) for the plant.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The main function of leaves is to perform photosynthesis, which is the process of converting light energy into chemical energy (sugar) for the plant.", "2.", "Sunlight is essential for photosynthesis, as it provides the energy needed to drive the chemical reactions.", "3.", "Trees grow taller to reach higher levels of sunlight, especially in dense forests where sunlight is limited.", "4.", "By growing leaves at the top of the tree, the leaves can capture more sunlight and maximize the plant's ability to perform photosynthesis."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lamb