 looking for a substance that can dissolve in water and form ions, as ions are responsible for conducting electricity in a solution.\n4. Table salt (sodium chloride) is an ionic compound that dissociates into sodium (Na+) and chloride (Cl-) ions when dissolved in water.\n5. Granulated sugar (sucrose) is a covalent compound that does not dissociate into ions when dissolved in water.\n6. Carbon dioxide (CO2) is a covalent compound that dissolves in water to form carbonic acid (H2CO3), but it does not produce a significant number of ions.\n7. Motor oil is a nonpolar substance that does not dissolve in water and does not produce ions.", "new_cot_probs": [1.3004844731767662e-05, 1.4163415995582795e-09, 3.160285644288052e-10, 7.051549621994724e-11], "cot_prob": [-0.29711830615997314], "cot_step_prob": [-0.3623872697353363], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 371, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 362, "step_token_count": 20}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [-0.00850682333111763, 0.8517045378684998, 0.7700042724609375, 0.7397489547729492, 0.6918037533760071, 0.6808363795280457, 0.6314379572868347, 0.6046788096427917, 0.6336674094200134, 0.6261491775512695, 0.6184482574462891, 0.6296806335449219, 0.6156416535377502, 0.5947185158729553, 0.6057987213134766, 0.5544416308403015, 0.5698323249816895, 0.5762430429458618, 0.576614260673523, 0.6348931789398193, 0.6058225631713867, 0.5969783067703247, 0.6107911467552185, 0.6272529363632202, 0.6143261194229126, 0.6755954623222351, 0.691236138343811, 0.7034858465194702, 0.7527704834938049, 0.7709415555000305, 0.7906607389450073, 0.8148099184036255, 0.6248236894607544], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999752044677734, 0.999934196472168, 0.999851405620575, 0.9998363852500916, 0.9997369050979614, 0.9997583627700806, 0.9996606111526489, 0.999542772769928, 0.9994533061981201, 0.9993830323219299, 0.9992567300796509, 0.9986693263053894, 0.9986939430236816, 0.998797595500946, 0.99