ntain, the air pressure is lower than at the bottom of the valley due to the difference in altitude.\n6. According to the principle of buoyancy, an object (or in this case, a parcel of air) will rise if it is less dense than the surrounding medium.\n7. Therefore, the cold air at the top of the mountain is less dense than the warmer air in the valley.", "new_cot_probs": [4.19854222855065e-06, 1.5142308740223598e-08, 5.570543581967513e-09, 3.3123663534251335e-11], "cot_prob": [-2.5538089275360107], "cot_step_prob": [-7.762288570404053], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 173, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 164, "step_token_count": 12}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.0026008719578385353, 0.8342317938804626, 0.7570880651473999, 0.7219973802566528, 0.6767895221710205, 0.6651105284690857, 0.6165715456008911, 0.5925517678260803, 0.6242814064025879, 0.6167858839035034, 0.6014472842216492, 0.6294740438461304, 0.6090861558914185, 0.5866091847419739, 0.5926011204719543, 0.5582385659217834, 0.5605550408363342, 0.5617562532424927, 0.5705578923225403, 0.6093863844871521, 0.5932677388191223, 0.5965631604194641, 0.6000393629074097, 0.6353216767311096, 0.6278002262115479, 0.6904376745223999, 0.7103403210639954, 0.7268064022064209, 0.7719635963439941, 0.7952525019645691, 0.8091467618942261, 0.8303806781768799, 0.6569327116012573], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.999962568283081, 0.9999033212661743, 0.9998524188995361, 0.9998242855072021, 0.9996800422668457, 0.999673068523407, 0.9995615482330322, 0.9993057250976562, 0.999215304851532, 0.9988729357719421, 0.99886554479599, 0.9989228844642639, 0.9986713528633118, 0.9984140992164612, 0.9977911710739136, 0.9970462918281555, 0.9958981275558472, 0.9932925701141357, 0.9936516284942627, 0.993664562702179, 0.9938436150550842, 0.9944494962692261, 0.9950504302978516, 0.9951015710830688, 0.995780348777771, 0.9960854053497314, 0.9961090087890625, 0.9966616630554199, 0.99699556827