 A hot plate (B) is an electrically heated, flat surface that can be used to support a cup or container. It provides a stable and controlled heat source, which can be used to place the cup of water on. By using a hot plate, we can directly measure the time it takes for the cup of water to boil.\n5. A stopwatch (C) is a tool used to measure the duration of an event or activity. While it can be used to manually record the time it takes for the cup of water to boil, it may not provide the most accurate or convenient method, especially if the cup is placed on a hot plate.\n6. A thermometer (D) is a tool used to measure temperature. It can be used to monitor the temperature of the cup of water as it heats up. However, it does not directly provide the time it takes for the cup of water to reach its boiling point.", "new_cot_probs": [1.1302572602289729e-05, 0.008518796414136887, 1.644514486542903e-05, 2.711346314754337e-05], "cot_prob": [-1.6982840299606323], "cot_step_prob": [-5.02718448638916], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 195, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 178, "step_token_count": 21}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.2286911904811859, 0.8904064893722534, 0.8093447685241699, 0.7806792259216309, 0.7398728132247925, 0.7313213348388672, 0.6811596155166626, 0.6741135716438293, 0.6985066533088684, 0.6919187307357788, 0.6810510754585266, 0.6855508089065552, 0.6671323776245117, 0.6547892689704895, 0.6685107946395874, 0.6236007809638977, 0.6399527192115784, 0.6581166982650757, 0.6551513671875, 0.7088993191719055, 0.7076034545898438, 0.7085604667663574, 0.7137337327003479, 0.7419108748435974, 0.7514162063598633, 0.7959783673286438, 0.8071290850639343, 0.8060027360916138, 0.8367571234703064, 0.8423929810523987, 0.8481243848800659, 0.8532819747924805, 0.835279107093811], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999489784240723, 0.9998499155044556, 0.9995318651199341, 0.9995297789573669, 0.9993430376052856, 0.9993014