elated to communication, camouflage, or predation.\n5. Moving through the water (A) is not directly related to producing light.\n6. Producing oxygen (B) is not a function of bioluminescence.\n7. Attracting prey (C) is a common reason for bioluminescence in deep-sea creatures. They use their light to lure or attract prey towards them.\n8. Escaping predators (D) is another reason for bioluminescence. Some organisms use their light to confuse or distract predators, allowing them to escape.", "new_cot_probs": [2.4808100462792027e-08, 5.5354356653936065e-09, 4.172080934949918e-06, 5.951154591343766e-08], "cot_prob": [-0.3336241543292999], "cot_step_prob": [-0.5737046003341675], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 337, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 321, "step_token_count": 24}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.004646523389965296, 0.8579102754592896, 0.77461838722229, 0.7445842623710632, 0.6980381608009338, 0.6989096403121948, 0.6508435606956482, 0.6264817118644714, 0.6586220860481262, 0.6492596864700317, 0.6475635170936584, 0.6434310674667358, 0.6385374069213867, 0.6151983141899109, 0.6377815008163452, 0.5905051231384277, 0.6060053706169128, 0.6069321036338806, 0.5925140976905823, 0.647757351398468, 0.6456245183944702, 0.6322957277297974, 0.6325477361679077, 0.6634817719459534, 0.6761163473129272, 0.7308410406112671, 0.7425169944763184, 0.7495521306991577, 0.79270339012146, 0.7980905771255493, 0.8218692541122437, 0.8385043740272522, 0.6284881830215454], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999578595161438, 0.999911904335022, 0.9998409152030945, 0.9997864961624146, 0.9995670914649963, 0.999458372592926, 0.9993526935577393, 0.9991946220397949, 0.9992038607597351, 0.9990765452384949, 0.9991522431373596, 0.9989280700683594, 0.9988667964935303, 0.9988603591918945, 0.9985948801040649, 0.9986014366149902, 0.998485803604126, 0.9984030723571777, 0.9984468221664429, 0.9983221888542175, 0.998312771320343, 0.9976894259452