{"id": "Mercury_414099", "question": "A student examined diagrams of two different cells. One cell was prokaryotic, and the other cell was eukaryotic. What should the student do to identify a major difference between the diagrams?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): compare the shapes of the two cells", "B): check to see which diagram shows a nucleus", "C): check to see which diagram shows cytoplasm", "D): compare the number of vacuoles in the two cells"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The question asks for a major difference between prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells.\n2. Prokaryotic cells are simpler and do not have a nucleus, while eukaryotic cells have a nucleus.\n3. The presence of a nucleus is a defining feature of eukaryotic cells.\n4. Therefore, the student should check to see which diagram shows a nucleus to identify the major difference.", "initial_cot_probs": [3.849014440504561e-09, 5.142178270034492e-05, 2.645386576460851e-09, 1.2495919854416115e-09], "initial_probs": [6.017066311869712e-08, 0.00026097625959664583, 4.686096133355022e-08, 8.754779656783285e-08], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_414099_step_1", "global_job_index": 434, "cot_step": "The question asks for a major difference between prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The question asks for a major difference between prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells.", "2.", "Prokaryotic cells are simpler and do not have a nucleus, while eukaryotic cells have a nucleus.", "3.", "The presence of a nucleus is a defining feature of eukaryotic cells.", "4.", "Therefore, the student should check to see which diagram shows a nucleus to identify the major difference."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}, "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_414