, 1.3654528174811276e-06]], "new_cot": "1. Millions of years ago, the Earth was covered with vast oceans and seas.\n2. These oceans and seas were home to a wide variety of plants and animals, including tiny marine organisms like plankton and algae.\n3. Over time, these plants and animals lived, grew, and eventually died.\n4. When these organisms died, their bodies sank to the bottom of the ocean or sea.\n5. As more and more plants and animals died, their bodies accumulated on the ocean floor, creating a thick layer of organic material.\n6. Over time, more sediments, such as sand, mud, and rocks, also settled on the ocean floor, creating a layer of rock and sediment.\n7. As the layers of rock and sediment piled up, they began to press down on the organic material and dead organisms trapped beneath them.\n8. This pressure, combined with the Earth's natural geological processes, caused the rock and sediment to slowly harden and compact over millions of years.\n9. As the rock and sediment continued to accumulate, the layers beneath them became increasingly dense and heavy.\n10. Eventually, the rock and sediment layers became so thick and heavy that they began to form a solid rock called sedimentary rock.\n11. The organic material and dead organisms that were", "new_cot_probs": [2.0986051652016613e-07, 3.0534525308212324e-07, 0.0005520771373994648, 3.646828972136973e-08], "cot_prob": [-2.1518466472625732], "cot_step_prob": [-5.317971706390381], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 209, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 190, "step_token_count": 21}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.014616223983466625, 0.8473584651947021, 0.7738962173461914, 0.7327512502670288, 0.6779642105102539, 0.6606654524803162, 0.6136588454246521, 0.5865409970283508, 0.6022862792015076, 0.5958296060562134, 0.5975966453552246, 0.6028174757957458, 0.5740382671356201, 0.5534109473228455, 0.554818332195282, 0.5279093384742737, 0.532694399356842, 0.53168