2333e-07, 4.6673442000155774e-08], [1.0797027243825141e-05, 4.2703071812866256e-05, 4.186461524113838e-07, 0.0004051554424222559], [4.435269147506915e-07, 0.0005511479103006423, 3.9141113461482746e-07, 7.312523280234018e-07]], "new_cot": "1. The Periodic Table of Elements is organized based on atomic structure, specifically the number of protons in the nucleus of an atom.\n2. Elements are arranged in increasing order of their atomic number, which is the number of protons in the nucleus.\n3. Elements on the left side of the Periodic Table have fewer protons in their nuclei compared to elements on the right side.\n4. The main distinction between elements on the left and right sides of the Periodic Table is the number of valence electrons (electrons in the outermost shell). Elements on the left have fewer valence electrons, while elements on the right have more.\n5. As you move from left to right across a period (row), each element has one more proton and one more electron than the element before it.\n6. This increase in the number of protons and electrons results in a stronger attraction between the positively charged nucleus and the negatively charged electrons, making it more difficult for the atom to lose electrons and form positive ions.", "new_cot_probs": [0.0009086228674277663, 6.002045438435744e-08, 4.125141472854921e-08, 6.326108970000632e-09], "cot_prob": [-1.6128618717193604], "cot_step_prob": [-5.052469730377197], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 212, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 193, "step_token_count": 21}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.016928404569625854, 0.8487242460250854, 0.7703744769096375, 0.7410444617271423, 0.7082962989807129, 0.7039737701416016, 0.6572908163070679, 0.6454089283943176, 0.6710554957389832, 0.6562987565994263, 0.6514315605163574, 0.661821722984314, 0.6503103971481323, 0.6286930441856384, 0.640443742275238, 0.6058048605918884, 0.622101366519928, 0.6263623833656311, 0.628