{"id": "Mercury_7086695", "question": "Which process is included in the formation of both metamorphic and sedimentary rock?", "step_idx": 3, "options": ["A): heating", "B): recrystallization", "C): compaction", "D): weathering"], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Metamorphic rocks are formed from pre-existing rocks (either igneous, sedimentary, or other metamorphic rocks) that undergo changes due to high temperature, pressure, or chemically active fluids.\n2. Sedimentary rocks are formed from the accumulation and lithification of sediments, which can be derived from weathering and erosion of pre-existing rocks.\n3. Compaction is a process that occurs during the formation of sedimentary rocks, as layers of sediments are compressed and squeezed together by the weight of overlying materials.\n4. Recrystallization is a process that occurs during the formation of metamorphic rocks, as minerals in the original rock change their crystal structure and size due to high temperature and pressure.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.958567790756206e-07, 7.097235652508971e-07, 1.830401197366882e-05, 5.8257658253069167e-08], "initial_probs": [5.975383828626946e-06, 0.00010591620957711712, 0.00019787753990385681, 1.1766228453780059e-06], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7086695_step_3", "global_job_index": 978, "cot_step": "Sedimentary rocks are formed from the accumulation and lithification of sediments, which can be derived from weathering and erosion of pre-existing rocks.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Metamorphic rocks are formed from pre-existing rocks (either igneous, sedimentary, or other metamorphic rocks) that undergo changes due to high temperature, pressure, or chemically active fluids.", "2.", "Sedimentary rocks are formed from the accumulation and lithification of sediments, which can be derived from weathering and erosion of pre-existing rocks.", "3.", "Compaction is a process that occurs during the formation of sedimentary rocks, as layers of sediments are compressed and squeezed together by the weight of overlying materials.", "4.", "Recrystallization is a process that occurs during the formation of metamorphic rocks, as minerals in the original rock change their crystal structure and size due to high temperature and pressure."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}, "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7086695_step_3", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0005_rs=1001_pos=True_ff2=False_critical_lora_causal_cot_i09_unfiltered_pos_s0/Mercury_7086695_step_3.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7086695", "step_idx": 3, "target_index": 125, "global_job_index": 978, "question": "Which process is included in the formation of both metamorphic and sedimentary rock?", "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0005_rs=1001_pos=True_ff2=False_critical_lora_causal_cot_i09_unfiltered_pos_s0/Mercury_7086695_step_3.json", "adapter_training_history": [{"epoch": 1, "mean_loss": 15.249238014221191, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 2, "mean_loss": 1.7209440469741821, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 3, "mean_loss": 0.048000823706388474, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 4, "mean_loss": 0.06711430102586746, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 5, "mean_loss": 0.06350163370370865, "evaluation": {"completion": "B) recrystallization.\n\n", "probs": [3.442337970227527e-07, 2