 between the atmosphere, biosphere, geosphere, and hydrosphere.\n2. Emission of waste (A) refers to the release of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases into the atmosphere, which is a relatively quick process.\n3. Respiration in animals (B) is the process by which animals convert organic matter into energy, releasing carbon dioxide as a byproduct. This process occurs continuously and is also relatively quick.\n4. Photosynthesis in plants (C) is the process by which plants convert carbon dioxide and sunlight into energy, storing carbon in their tissues. This process is ongoing and relatively quick.\n5. Formation of fossil fuels (D) is the process by which organic matter is buried and transformed into coal, oil, and natural gas over millions of years. This process takes the longest time to complete among the given options.", "new_cot_probs": [1.4162799821804128e-09, 1.4162799821804128e-09, 3.3974794089175475e-09, 1.8921115042758174e-05], "cot_prob": [-0.34166985750198364], "cot_step_prob": [-0.2894815504550934], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 308, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 282, "step_token_count": 33}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.14451581239700317, 0.8760594129562378, 0.7904916405677795, 0.7583338618278503, 0.70902019739151, 0.6968071460723877, 0.6428393125534058, 0.6201600432395935, 0.6535114049911499, 0.6515236496925354, 0.6445418000221252, 0.6435608863830566, 0.6287581920623779, 0.6058776378631592, 0.6204941272735596, 0.5793554186820984, 0.5822789669036865, 0.6007250547409058, 0.6050676703453064, 0.6495869159698486, 0.6361368894577026, 0.6360810995101929, 0.6242765784263611, 0.6475620865821838, 0.6624488830566406, 0.7125082015991211, 0.7270804643630981, 0.7234233617782593, 0.7724248766899109, 0.7904688119888306, 0.8147774934768677, 0.8398889303207397, 0.694617509841919], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999347925186157, 0.9998658895492554, 0.9997350573539734, 0.999690055847168, 0.