{"id": "ACTAAP_2011_5_16", "question": "Pat dissolves some table salt in water. She then puts a drop of the water on a microscope slide and turns on the lamp. As the water evaporates, Pat observes small cubic structures being formed. What process is Pat seeing through the microscope?", "step_idx": 5, "options": ["A): purification of an ore", "B): the growth of a crystal", "C): a liquid becoming a solid", "D): sedimentation of granules"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. Pat dissolves table salt (sodium chloride) in water.\n2. She places a drop of this saltwater solution on a microscope slide.\n3. As the water evaporates, the salt remains behind.\n4. Small cubic structures are observed forming.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.0585280147145113e-09, 1.890139901661314e-05, 3.2200798472104e-08, 1.1018507217741558e-09], "initial_probs": [3.204047516192077e-08, 0.000108228501630947, 1.0610348226691713e-06, 5.2825814833568074e-08], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "ACTAAP_2011_5_16_step_5", "global_job_index": 458, "cot_step": "As the water evaporates, the salt remains behind.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Pat dissolves table salt (sodium chloride) in water.", "2.", "She places a drop of this saltwater solution on a microscope slide.", "3.", "As the water evaporates, the salt remains behind.", "4.", "Small cubic structures are observed forming."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}, "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "ACTAAP_2011_5_16_step_5", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0005_rs=1001_pos=True_ff2=False_critical_lora_causal_cot_i09_unfiltered_pos_s0/ACTAAP_2011_5_16_step_5.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentenciz