95850688126e-07], [1.5198642344671498e-08, 1.8515736144308903e-07, 2.8394799400643933e-08, 0.0001231558562722057], [0.00011521431588334963, 5.335481318979873e-07, 1.0716600627347361e-05, 1.7321772816103476e-07], [1.201728878186259e-06, 0.00015739540685899556, 1.43526051488152e-07, 2.6814194598046015e-07], [0.0001229871268151328, 2.3742101973311946e-07, 8.734231471407838e-08, 1.7198722446210013e-08], [1.5058070630402653e-06, 5.255782525637187e-06, 1.2360416690171405e-07, 9.316098294220865e-05], [4.123879193684843e-08, 5.8068537327926606e-05, 9.892671926081675e-08, 1.4393752678643068e-07]], "new_cot": "1. The question states that there is too little water in the body.\n2. The kidneys are responsible for filtering blood and producing urine.\n3. Antidiuretic hormone (ADH) is a hormone that regulates the kidneys' ability to filter and reabsorb water.\n4. When there is too little water in the body, the hypothalamus in the brain detects this and signals the pituitary gland to release more ADH.\n5. The kidneys respond to the increased levels of ADH by reabsorbing more water from the urine, which results in the production of a smaller volume of more concentrated urine.\n6. The concentration of urine in the kidneys triggers the sensation of thirst, which prompts the person to drink more water.", "new_cot_probs": [2.1970774469082244e-05, 9.158780812867917e-06, 2.270234844559127e-08, 6.504331739876079e-09], "cot_prob": [-1.5553481578826904], "cot_step_prob": [-4.944915294647217], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 278, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 256, "step_token_count": 26}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.012923086062073708, 0.8638480305671692, 0.7590183019638062, 0.4681454002857208, 0.4603112041950226, 0.5135646462440491, 0.5082354545593262, 0.5098559856414795, 0.6390424966812134, 0.612689733505249, 0.61262446641922, 0.6254221200942993, 0.6025748252868652, 0.5763605237007141, 0.5899519324302673, 0.5394260883331299,