) relative to the ground decreases.\n4. Simultaneously, the sled's kinetic energy (energy of motion) - which depends on both its mass and the square of its velocity - increases because it's moving faster.\n5. At the bottom of the hill, the sled reaches its maximum kinetic energy (as it's at its lowest point and moving at its highest velocity) and minimum potential energy (since it's closest to the ground).", "new_cot_probs": [2.2397803149942774e-06, 0.004049617797136307, 6.417078566300916e-07, 6.417078566300916e-07], "cot_prob": [-2.29461407661438], "cot_step_prob": [-5.2375407218933105], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 245, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 226, "step_token_count": 23}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.04291108623147011, 0.855650782585144, 0.788161039352417, 0.7648699283599854, 0.7327455282211304, 0.7315236330032349, 0.6884021759033203, 0.6668666005134583, 0.6992189288139343, 0.6986660957336426, 0.6937661170959473, 0.6794838905334473, 0.6505355834960938, 0.6301796436309814, 0.6620755195617676, 0.6176341772079468, 0.6057313680648804, 0.6005839109420776, 0.5954037308692932, 0.6423285603523254, 0.6171044111251831, 0.6123263239860535, 0.5800062417984009, 0.6167190074920654, 0.6293671131134033, 0.6760318279266357, 0.6894475221633911, 0.6917198300361633, 0.7316886782646179, 0.7494982481002808, 0.7754570245742798, 0.7947242259979248, 0.6057295799255371], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999463558197021, 0.9998912215232849, 0.9997988343238831, 0.9997594356536865, 0.9994320273399353, 0.9993954300880432, 0.998870313167572, 0.998881459236145, 0.9989157915115356, 0.998878002166748, 0.9986775517463684, 0.9988603591918945, 0.9987218379974365, 0.9985442757606506, 0.9979121088981628, 0.9976379871368408, 0.9966628551483154, 0.9961885809898376, 0.996497631072998, 0.9965718984603882, 0.9965132474899292, 0.9967828989028931, 0.9968464374542236, 0.9964450597763062, 0.9969490766525269, 0.9968324899673462,