y and urinate less.\n(C): You get hungry and sweat more.\n(D): You get hungry and sweat less.\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\n1.\nWhen you have too little water in your body, your kidneys excrete antidiuretic hormone (ADH).\n2.\nADH is a hormone that helps the body retain water by reducing the amount of water excreted in urine.\n3.", "specificity_preds": [1, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 2, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 3, 0, 1, 0, 3, 1], "specificity_probs": [[5.345408226276049e-06, 0.008529089391231537, 9.986536497308407e-06, 6.0571410358534195e-06], [1.6374913684558123e-05, 3.466569251031615e-05, 0.01089163776487112, 3.466569251031615e-05], [0.0014928700402379036, 1.0058878615382127e-05, 1.5425792980749975e-06, 3.441959393057914e-07], [2.2976611944613978e-05, 0.0016107847914099693, 0.005622191354632378, 6.24569074716419e-05], [0.00403725728392601, 1.6499347111675888e-05, 2.867156808861182e-06, 1.4560621821146924e-05], [0.00015169582911767066, 0.00019478131434880197, 0.005023476202040911, 1.4109909898252226e-05], [0.0030238786712288857, 4.313331373850815e-05, 0.00011724849900929257, 1.7980639313464053e-05], [2.87967782242049e-06, 5.379946287575876e-06, 0.004054888151586056, 6.907987881277222e-06], [1.722392516967375e-05, 0.0006463230238296092, 0.007873826660215855, 2.5060664484044537e-05], [0.00391450896859169, 9.206042159348726e-05, 5.583746678894386e-05, 9.206042159348726e-05], [0.0024263658560812473, 0.0011461342219263315, 0.0011461342219263315, 0.0005413953913375735], [0.00048551784129813313, 0.005914818495512009, 0.003587518585845828, 0.0006234172033146024], [1.0754223694675602e-05, 9.004400635603815e-05, 0.010407673195004463, 0.0005181675078347325], [0.0066032130271196365, 7.33550768927671e-05, 1.44444684337941e-05, 2.6985822842107154e-05], [2.8682409265456954e-06, 3.083649426116608e-05, 3.2501427540410077e-06, 0.006658828817307949], [0.005846651736646891, 5.0583446864038706e-05, 0.0007912582368589938, 1.2789498214260675e-05], [5.7155029935529456e-05, 0.008482558652758598, 8.765007805777714e-06, 1.4451054084929638e-05], [0.005170946009457111, 1.6457986930618063e-05, 5.343126304069301e-06, 9.284961492994626e-07], [0.00031175650656223297, 0.0005139995482750237, 9.414229680260178e-06, 0.008040306158363819], [4.178260041953763e-06, 0.004043617285788059, 7.806016583344899e-06, 1.1357687981217168e-05]], "new_cot": "1. When you have too little water in your body, your brain releases antidiuretic hormone (ADH).\n2. ADH acts on the kidneys, signaling them to retain more water by increasing the permeability of the kidney tubules.\n3. This causes the kidneys to reabsorb more water back into the bloodstream, reducing the amount of water lost through urine.\n4. As a result, the concentration of urine increases, making it more concentrated and reducing the volume of urine produced.\n5. The release of ADH also triggers the sensation of thirst, prompting you to drink more water to rehydrate your body.", "new_cot_probs": [0.00041012995643541217, 0.008237680420279503, 3.548319455148885e-06, 1.8992786863236688e-06], "cot_prob": [-1.606130599975586], "cot_step_prob": [-4.9991044998168945], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 278, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 262, "step_token_count": 20}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.03280118107795715, 0.8676220178604126, 0.7872114181518555, 0.7621906399726868, 0.7234444618225098, 0.7075509428977966, 0.6524582505226135, 0.633946418762207, 0.6475902795791626, 0.6378766894340515, 0.6474026441574097, 0.6581705808639526, 0.6417631506919861, 0.6315972208976746, 0.64736008644104, 0.6000528931617737, 0.6025182604789734, 0.6067735552787781, 0.6149063110351562, 0.666012704372406, 0.6392124891281128, 0.632036566734314, 0.6238254904747009, 0.6435306072235107, 0.6586434245109558, 0.7083631753921509, 0.7169883251190186, 0.7229304313659668, 0.7577864527702332, 0.7791630029678345, 0.794628918170929, 0.8100508451461792, 0.7178962230682373], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer":