tary rocks are formed from the accumulation and lithification of sediments, which can be derived from the weathering and erosion of pre-existing rocks.\n3. Compaction is a process that occurs during the formation of sedimentary rocks, as layers of sediments are compressed and squeezed together by the weight of overlying materials.\n4. Recrystallization is a process that occurs during the formation of metamorphic rocks, as minerals within the rock change their crystal structure and size due to high temperature and pressure.", "new_cot_probs": [3.324479109778622e-07, 7.975010589689191e-07, 2.0567822502925992e-05, 6.5462877785194e-08], "cot_prob": [-0.3558555245399475], "cot_step_prob": [-0.4224463999271393], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 278, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 244, "step_token_count": 38}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.02789064310491085, 0.8623451590538025, 0.7714746594429016, 0.6139618754386902, 0.5961854457855225, 0.6229192018508911, 0.5862159729003906, 0.5607249736785889, 0.6236964464187622, 0.6306476593017578, 0.625717043876648, 0.6350318789482117, 0.6229073405265808, 0.6040852069854736, 0.615529477596283, 0.5871148109436035, 0.5754665732383728, 0.5781305432319641, 0.5846670866012573, 0.6340369582176208, 0.6243071556091309, 0.6230698823928833, 0.6120969653129578, 0.6478493809700012, 0.6564655303955078, 0.7017459273338318, 0.7145180702209473, 0.7185523509979248, 0.7642776966094971, 0.7828007936477661, 0.8058762550354004, 0.8278839588165283, 0.6450302004814148], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999579787254333, 0.9998679757118225, 0.9997607469558716, 0.999745786190033, 0.999341607093811, 0.9992803335189819, 0.9985215663909912, 0.9985182285308838, 0.9985257983207703, 0.9985939264297485, 0.9983141422271729, 0.9986515045166016, 0.9985002279281616, 0.9983348846435547, 0.9960439205169678, 0.9936728477478027, 0.9882254600524902, 0.9854778051376343, 0.98240065574646, 0.9723618030548096,