, 0, 2, 0, 2, 2, 0, 1, 1, 2, 0, 3, 0, 1, 0, 3, 1], "specificity_probs": [[0.0003801705897785723, 0.09302467852830887, 0.00023058510851114988, 0.00013985694386065006], [0.0005012864130549133, 0.00030404559220187366, 0.0743975043296814, 0.00030404559220187366], [0.03683725371956825, 0.0005254551651887596, 9.131042315857485e-05, 1.5867371985223144e-05], [0.0004019465413875878, 0.010366338305175304, 0.03618207573890686, 0.001801399514079094], [0.022739078849554062, 9.292941831517965e-05, 1.6148711438290775e-05, 5.636454079649411e-05], [0.0013864059001207352, 0.0006548917735926807, 0.03575588017702103, 8.862996764946729e-05], [0.016621101647615433, 0.0005019137752242386, 0.0010625513968989253, 0.00023708725348114967], [7.143428229028359e-05, 5.5633070587646216e-05, 0.03700387105345726, 5.5633070587646216e-05], [0.000287705915980041, 0.004500477574765682, 0.03325428068637848, 0.0002240655740024522], [0.027948470786213875, 0.0005118941189721227, 0.0003986635128967464, 0.0010836797300726175], [0.012347877956926823, 0.020358208566904068, 0.009616537019610405, 0.012347877956926823], [0.004222598858177662, 0.031201018020510674, 0.01473831757903099, 0.002561135683208704], [0.00017496485088486224, 0.0007841380429454148, 0.07058585435152054, 0.004512403160333633], [0.03642218932509422, 0.0008565678144805133, 0.00011592384544201195, 0.0001911261206259951], [4.357802026788704e-05, 0.0003220004145987332, 5.595528273261152e-05, 0.028985556215047836], [0.04592997953295708, 0.0003094737767241895, 0.0017808986594900489, 0.0001138490333687514], [0.001340663991868496, 0.07319777458906174, 0.00014130494673736393, 0.0002329724666196853], [0.0464385561645031, 0.00024368717276956886, 6.161376950331032e-05, 2.56844414252555e-05], [0.0016955079045146704, 0.0035893903113901615, 8.441436511930078e-05, 0.056147508323192596], [0.00014645879855379462, 0.059085696935653687, 0.00014645879855379462, 0.0002414697373751551]], "new_cot": "1. The process of electrolysis involves passing an electric current through water (H_{2}O).\n2. The electric current causes the water molecules to break apart due to the flow of electrons.\n3. As the electric current flows through the water, it creates a voltage difference between two electrodes submerged in the water.\n4. This voltage difference causes the water molecules to separate into their constituent elements - hydrogen (H) and oxygen (O).\n5. The electrode connected to the positive terminal of the power source attracts negatively charged hydrogen ions (H^{-}) from the water.\n6. These hydrogen ions gain electrons from the electrode, which converts them into neutral hydrogen atoms (H).\n7. Meanwhile, the electrode connected to the negative terminal of the power source attracts positively charged hydroxide ions (OH^{-}) from the water.\n8. These hydroxide ions lose electrons at the electrode, which converts them into neutral oxygen atoms (O).\n9. As more and more hydrogen and oxygen atoms are generated at the electrodes, they start to form bonds with each other.\n10. The hydrogen atoms bond together to form hydrogen gas (H_{2}), while the oxygen atoms bond together to form oxygen gas (O_{2}).\n11. The electrolysis process", "new_cot_probs": [0.0020741636399179697, 0.307833194732666, 0.0009797654347494245, 0.00028070752159692347], "cot_prob": [-1.8730312585830688], "cot_step_prob": [-2.9629898071289062], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 263, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 241, "step_token_count": 24}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.31136995553970337, 0.8926694393157959, 0.8168177008628845, 0.7866611480712891, 0.7513169646263123, 0.7480751276016235, 0.6951935887336731, 0.6768883466720581, 0.6928805112838745, 0.6759738326072693, 0.6664065718650818, 0.6685342788696289, 0.6515662670135498, 0.6352202892303467, 0.6567168831825256, 0.6129273772239685, 0.6167262196540833, 0.6209729313850403, 0.6344850659370422, 0.6865788698196411, 0.6648722887039185, 0.6712814569473267, 0.67