{"id": "Mercury_7142415", "question": "A lake that received runoff from surrounding farmland had a healthy fish population. Several years ago, a new type of pesticide was used to treat crops. As runoff entered the lake, it killed an insect that was a primary food source for fish. Which will most likely occur if farmers in the area stop using the pesticide?", "step_idx": 5, "options": ["A): The population of fish will increase.", "B): The insects will become more resistant to the pesticide.", "C): The lake will be unable to support life.", "D): The fish will find another food source."], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. The pesticide was killing the insects that were a primary food source for fish.\n2. If farmers stop using the pesticide, the insect population will likely recover.\n3. With more insects available as a food source, the fish population will have a better chance to thrive.", "initial_cot_probs": [3.534226925694384e-05, 4.361583094691923e-09, 1.604536503663212e-09, 4.597074387824307e-10], "initial_probs": [0.00042684967047534883, 2.2399015051632887e-06, 3.4350003375038796e-07, 1.9767062440223526e-06], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7142415_step_5", "global_job_index": 1616, "cot_step": "With more insects available as a food source, the fish population will have a better chance to thrive.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The pesticide was killing the insects that were a primary food source for fish.", "2.", "If farmers stop using the pesticide, the insect population will likely recover.", "3.", "With more insects available as a food source, the fish population will have a better chance to thrive."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}, "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7142415_step_5", "adapter_path": "../../..