804566025734], [3.3993586839642376e-05, 0.029032519087195396, 0.00011864926636917517, 7.196442311396822e-05]], "new_cot": "1. Jenny is walking on a hot day, which means the temperature outside is higher than the temperature inside the grocery store where the chocolate chips were initially stored.\n2. The environment around Jenny, including the air and the ground, is likely to be warmer than the temperature of the chocolate chips.\n3. When Jenny carries the bag with the chocolate chips, the heat from the environment will come into contact with the surface of the bag.\n4. The heat will then transfer from the warmer environment to the cooler surface of the bag.\n5. As the temperature of the bag increases, the heat will continue to transfer from the environment to the bag and eventually to the chocolate chips inside the bag.\n6. The heat transfer will cause the temperature of the chocolate chips to rise.\n7. As the temperature of the chocolate chips increases, they will reach their melting point.\n8. Once the temperature of the chocolate chips reaches their melting point, they will start to change from a solid state to a liquid state, resulting in the melting of the chocolate chips.", "new_cot_probs": [0.0029020956717431545, 2.2157773855724372e-05, 0.26123833656311035, 9.236733603756875e-06], "cot_prob": [-2.1125056743621826], "cot_step_prob": [-4.62077522277832], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 248, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 234, "step_token_count": 17}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.0343632809817791, 0.8540201783180237, 0.7719404101371765, 0.7324461340904236, 0.688380777835846, 0.6807570457458496, 0.6464905142784119, 0.628084659576416, 0.64915931224823, 0.6365792751312256, 0.6312393546104431, 0.6457490921020508, 0.6366667747497559, 0.6223956942558289, 0.6222284436225891, 0.5824815630912781, 0.58649080991745, 0.6029679179191589, 0.6170721650123596, 0.6563100218772888, 0.6269632577896118, 0.602582275867