{"id": "Mercury_7174213", "question": "The speed of a sound wave varies as it travels through different substances. Which factor will most affect the speed of a sound wave?", "step_idx": 7, "options": ["A): the frequency of the wave", "B): the wavelength of the wave", "C): the source that created the sound", "D): the distance between molecules in the medium"], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. The speed of a sound wave is determined by the properties of the medium through which it travels.\n2. The frequency and wavelength of a sound wave are related to each other by the equation v = f * \u03bb, where v is the speed of the wave, f is the frequency, and \u03bb is the wavelength.\n3. The source of the sound wave does not affect the speed of the wave itself, but rather the frequency and amplitude of the wave.\n4. The distance between molecules in the medium affects the speed of sound because it determines how easily the sound wave can propagate through the medium.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.3347386246541646e-09, 5.600746533218626e-09, 1.6046406425829218e-09, 1.6695590602466837e-05], "initial_probs": [2.0940808553859824e-07, 8.282250405500236e-07, 3.0468697787000565e-07, 0.00015783174603711814], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7174213_step_7", "global_job_index": 330, "cot_step": "The distance between molecules in the medium affects the speed of sound because it determines how easily the sound wave can propagate through the medium.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The speed of a sound wave is determined by the properties of the medium through which it travels.", "2.", "The frequency and wavelength of a sound wave are related to each other by the equation v = f * \u03bb, where v is the speed of the wave, f is the frequency, and \u03bb is the wavelength.", "3.", "The source of the sound wave does not affect the speed of the wave itself, but rather the frequency and amplitude of the wave.", "4.", "The distance between molecules in the medium affects t