tions given are leaching of soils, evaporation rates, runoff from rains, and amounts of sunlight.\n4. Leaching of soils refers to the loss of nutrients from the soil due to water movement. This would likely decrease productivity.\n5. Evaporation rates refer to the amount of water that evaporates from the soil and plants. High evaporation rates can lead to water stress and lower productivity.\n6. Runoff from rains refers to the movement of water over the land surface. This can lead to soil erosion and nutrient loss, which would decrease productivity.\n7. Amounts of sunlight refer to the amount of solar radiation that reaches the plants. Sunlight is essential for photosynthesis, which is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy.\n8. Considering the options, the factor that most likely accounts for the high productivity of some areas in mountain valleys is (D) amounts of sunlight.", "new_cot_probs": [1.1029905877535384e-09, 1.6048417039726814e-09, 1.2498519996739788e-09, 1.6697682440280914e-05], "cot_prob": [-0.30914852023124695], "cot_step_prob": [-0.4357372224330902], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 392, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 384, "step_token_count": 20}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [-0.00146494060754776, 0.850013017654419, 0.7685602307319641, 0.7366557121276855, 0.6875355839729309, 0.6860393285751343, 0.6349039673805237, 0.6152838468551636, 0.656212568283081, 0.6509969234466553, 0.6491309404373169, 0.6307708024978638, 0.6051146388053894, 0.5890685319900513, 0.620756983757019, 0.569266676902771, 0.5818392634391785, 0.5861236453056335, 0.5929683446884155, 0.6462377905845642, 0.6381822824478149, 0.6329066753387451, 0.6227666735649109, 0.645373523235321, 0.6559929847717285, 0.7108819484710693, 0.728291928768158, 0.7247344851493835, 0.7708964943885803, 0.7803113460540771, 0.8075276017189026, 0.8330978751182556, 0.6996201276779175], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0