 valleys.\n2. Productivity in agriculture is generally influenced by factors such as soil fertility, water availability, sunlight, and temperature.\n3. Among the given options, leaching of soils (A) and runoff from rains (C) are processes that can actually decrease soil fertility by removing essential nutrients.\n4. Evaporation rates (B) are related to the phase change of water from liquid to gas and do not directly affect crop productivity.\n5. The remaining option, amounts of sunlight (D), is a crucial factor for photosynthesis, which is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy to fuel their growth.", "new_cot_probs": [1.1512103770261461e-11, 4.846776452405166e-11, 2.5942926626387752e-11, 4.4503084950520133e-07], "cot_prob": [-0.8495239615440369], "cot_step_prob": [-5.146279335021973], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 392, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 384, "step_token_count": 20}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [-0.00146494060754776, 0.8515269160270691, 0.7736313343048096, 0.7392794489860535, 0.6891037225723267, 0.6894326210021973, 0.6437859535217285, 0.6272600293159485, 0.656679630279541, 0.6527276039123535, 0.647343635559082, 0.6327943801879883, 0.6081624031066895, 0.5956144332885742, 0.6227241158485413, 0.5666399002075195, 0.5767416954040527, 0.5655685067176819, 0.5682191252708435, 0.6077809929847717, 0.598472535610199, 0.5973972082138062, 0.5815799236297607, 0.6088957190513611, 0.6159816384315491, 0.6718456745147705, 0.6945596933364868, 0.690234363079071, 0.7378377914428711, 0.7496057748794556, 0.7808141112327576, 0.8098480701446533, 0.6357421875], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999505281448364, 0.9998534321784973, 0.9995468854904175, 0.9995169639587402, 0.9993216395378113, 0.9993486404418945, 0.9991514086723328, 0.9991234540939331, 0.9991706609725952, 0.999117910861969, 0.9989404678344727, 0.9991623163223267, 0.9987789392471313, 0.9984920620918274, 0.998174905