f from a river can create valleys and canyons, but it is not the primary process for forming plateaus.\n4. (B) Weathering by waves can shape coastal landforms, but it does not typically create plateaus.\n5. (C) Erosion of rock debris can contribute to the formation of plateaus by wearing away surrounding areas and leaving the elevated flat surface exposed.\n6. (D) A buildup of cooled lava can create volcanic plateaus, which are formed by successive layers of lava flows that solidify and build up over time.", "new_cot_probs": [1.2597124232627266e-08, 5.251262535921342e-09, 3.492833457130473e-06, 7.394327440124471e-06], "cot_prob": [-0.3590865135192871], "cot_step_prob": [-0.4589717984199524], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 303, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 274, "step_token_count": 34}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.11476363241672516, 0.86956787109375, 0.765150249004364, 0.5017004609107971, 0.5017472505569458, 0.5523284077644348, 0.544198215007782, 0.543786346912384, 0.6609871983528137, 0.6681779623031616, 0.6641733050346375, 0.6591223478317261, 0.6433159708976746, 0.6137132048606873, 0.652431845664978, 0.6131415963172913, 0.6394075751304626, 0.6456842422485352, 0.6477288603782654, 0.6936933994293213, 0.6883679032325745, 0.6856955885887146, 0.6791580319404602, 0.7037666440010071, 0.7213338017463684, 0.7619273662567139, 0.782288134098053, 0.7914440631866455, 0.8264340758323669, 0.8328448534011841, 0.8516392111778259, 0.8623790144920349, 0.6893056631088257], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999264478683472, 0.999823808670044, 0.9981039762496948, 0.9983053207397461, 0.9975446462631226, 0.9964004755020142, 0.9955724477767944, 0.9953247308731079, 0.9965007901191711, 0.9968624711036682, 0.9965679049491882, 0.9971010088920593, 0.9961961507797241, 0.9961881637573242, 0.9922472238540649, 0.9898650646209717, 0.9807619452476501, 0.972926676273346, 0.9728270173072815, 0.9684816002845764, 0.967233657836914