lyze new data as it becomes available\n   (D) delete earlier reports that were missing the new findings\n3. Option (A) suggests excluding research on teeth or bones, which would not be beneficial as these are important aspects of dinosaur research.\n4. Option (B) suggests predicting the next discovery, which is not directly related to reporting current research findings.\n5. Option (C) suggests analyzing new data as it becomes available, which is a logical and responsible approach to staying updated with the latest research findings.\n6. Option (D) suggests deleting earlier reports that were missing the new findings, which is not a constructive approach as it would erase valuable historical data.", "new_cot_probs": [1.7251228001669006e-08, 3.849268903621805e-09, 0.00012336259533185512, 2.060364989731056e-09], "cot_prob": [-0.3431355357170105], "cot_step_prob": [-0.7665506601333618], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 375, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 348, "step_token_count": 32}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.14467459917068481, 0.8699101805686951, 0.7924515008926392, 0.7668057084083557, 0.7254945039749146, 0.7208472490310669, 0.6893252730369568, 0.6829600930213928, 0.70902419090271, 0.719083845615387, 0.7146206498146057, 0.7095276117324829, 0.6999666094779968, 0.6782675981521606, 0.7096179723739624, 0.6684091687202454, 0.6810212731361389, 0.6865432262420654, 0.6845560073852539, 0.7249923348426819, 0.7157084941864014, 0.703448474407196, 0.6726824045181274, 0.7011386752128601, 0.7101858258247375, 0.7549945116043091, 0.7620909810066223, 0.7652060985565186, 0.8035935163497925, 0.8195337653160095, 0.8355671167373657, 0.8444005846977234, 0.6056552529335022], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9998956322669983, 0.9997609853744507, 0.9993373155593872, 0.999343991279602, 0.9989257454872131, 0.9987149238586426, 0.9987561106681824, 0.9986385107040405, 0.9986897706985474, 0.9986153841018677, 0.9984914660453796