 salt (sodium chloride) is an ionic compound that dissociates into sodium (Na+) and chloride (Cl-) ions when dissolved in water.\n5. Granulated sugar (sucrose) is a covalent compound that does not dissociate into ions when dissolved in water.\n6. Carbon dioxide (CO2) is a covalent compound that dissolves in water to form carbonic acid (H2CO3), but it does not produce a significant number of ions.\n7. Motor oil is a nonpolar substance that does not dissolve in water and does not produce ions.", "new_cot_probs": [1.3004844731767662e-05, 1.4163415995582795e-09, 3.160285644288052e-10, 7.051549621994724e-11], "cot_prob": [-0.29711830615997314], "cot_step_prob": [-0.4205024540424347], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 371, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 352, "step_token_count": 28}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.03539383038878441, 0.8651200532913208, 0.7867489457130432, 0.7563046216964722, 0.711836576461792, 0.7020992040634155, 0.6490116119384766, 0.628308117389679, 0.6672926545143127, 0.6650565266609192, 0.6653809547424316, 0.6746867895126343, 0.6577108502388, 0.6375054121017456, 0.6492365598678589, 0.5886673927307129, 0.6108442544937134, 0.6106810569763184, 0.6121294498443604, 0.6725761294364929, 0.6421964764595032, 0.6293942332267761, 0.6352261304855347, 0.6457270383834839, 0.6335496306419373, 0.6971015334129333, 0.7119690179824829, 0.7250567078590393, 0.7693461775779724, 0.7877306342124939, 0.8088828325271606, 0.8283158540725708, 0.6161276698112488], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999570250511169, 0.9998671412467957, 0.9997234344482422, 0.9996947646141052, 0.9995102882385254, 0.9993590116500854, 0.9988401532173157, 0.998640775680542, 0.9985378980636597, 0.9985723495483398, 0.9985384345054626, 0.9986043572425842, 0.9982764720916748, 0.9983534216880798, 0.9978809952735901, 0.997494637966156, 0.9970053434371948, 0.99717777967453, 0.9977830648422241, 0.9979408979415894, 0.9977362155914307, 0.99785917